# Navigation

Use the project's existing navigation system.

If Expo Router is installed, prefer file-based routing.

Typical structure:

```text
(auth)/
  welcome
  login
  signup
  otp
(onboarding)/
  languages
  proficiency
  goals
  interests
  profile
(app)/
  discover
  conversations
  notifications
  profile
conversation/
  [id]
profile/
  [id]
settings/
```

Do not blindly create this exact structure if the repository already has one.

## Auth routing

Unauthenticated users should not reach authenticated routes.

Authenticated users should not repeatedly see onboarding steps they already completed.

Use server-confirmed auth/session state.

## Deep links

Conversation/profile links must:
- validate the target resource
- handle missing/deleted resources
- respect blocks/privacy
- avoid exposing private route data

## Back behavior

Mobile back behavior should be predictable.
Do not intercept back navigation unless the screen has a clear reason.

Forms with unsaved changes should use the existing confirmation pattern if the app supports it.
